    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both its tests pass along with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation following the codebase's existing pattern for derived owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/CityRegions.java`** (new) \u2014 A small, single-responsibility class holding the fixed city-to-region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) with a static `regionOf(city)` that returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`. Keeping the table isolated avoids polluting the entity with lookup data and makes the rule reusable.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a transient `getLocality()` getter that delegates to `CityRegions.regionOf(city)`, mirroring the existing `getMembershipTier()`/`getInitials()` derived getters.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Declared `locality` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` schema. The build's OpenAPI generator produces the DTO field, and MapStruct auto-maps `getLocality()` \u2192 `locality`, so it surfaces at `$.locality` in the JSON response with no controller/mapper changes.\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass: `Sydney \u2192 NSW` and an unlisted city \u2192 `UNKNOWN`.",
